import json
P=Path(__file__).parent;x=json.loads((P/'comparison-manifest.json').read_text());groups={}
for f in x['families']:groups.setdefault(f['group'],[]).append(f)
T={1:'Summary surfaces',2:'Passage and citation controls',3:'Expanded evidence layouts',4:'Search and question-entry boxes',5:'Quick filters',6:'Filter options in panels',7:'Related topics, people and places',8:'Dropdowns and value pickers',9:'Tabs, switches and sliders',10:'Expand and inspect controls',11:'Reset, apply and utility actions',12:'Navigation and icon actions',13:'Text fields and note editors',14:'Dialogs and panels',15:'Cards and content blocks',16:'Keyboard focus cues'}
intent={1:'Different content roles can justify different emphasis; the amount of glass/spacing is a preference, not automatically a bug.',2:'Direct passage navigation, preview citations and plain inline links are distinct roles. Mixed sizes/corners within a role show drift.',3:'The Read/Marked quote-layout difference is verified. Different History comparisons contain other kinds of evidence.',4:'List-search shapes differ; Chat intentionally composes a question. Rounded box versus pill and magnifier use are independent choices.',5:'Category colors and the Women cue carry meaning; target size and selected feedback need consistent rules.',6:'Grid tiles versus quick-filter pills can be intentional. Prophecy panel tiles, Commandment facets and Marked category tiles differ in corners.',7:'Topic, person and place navigation can have distinct cues. Keep related controls recognizable without turning labels into fake buttons.',8:'Native selects and grid/step pickers behave differently by design; small cells and inconsistent touch targets are usability concerns.',9:'True tabs, toggles and sliders serve different jobs. Keep their keyboard semantics; choose a consistent visual treatment within each job.',10:'Native disclosure rows and tiny inner-card chevrons differ markedly in target size. Single activation versus summary double-click is also a behavior choice.',11:'Reset, Apply, Show results and outward links should not automatically have the same emphasis just because they share a pill skin.',12:'Header styling is shared; phone target size is small. Close buttons, floating actions and map controls vary in size and corner treatment.',13:'Title fields and multiline editors are separate roles. Shared note title styling already exists; editor layout and context vary.',14:'Centered dialog versus bottom sheet is a useful distinction; within each, corners, blur, padding and close targets vary.',15:'Different content can justify different internals. Compare shell, title and spacing separately rather than forcing every card into one layout.',16:'Search focus is present but varies in color, thickness and whether it surrounds the input or wrapper. Native disclosures use browser focus.'}
rec={1:'Keep glass as a selectable summary treatment; do not automatically apply it to every biography.',2:'Retain two role-based sizes if desired: roomy direct navigation and recognizable citations, with accessible hit areas.',3:'Prefer a responsive rule if both layouts are useful: beside on wide screens, above on narrow screens.',4:'Keep the Chat composer separate. Select a common list-search treatment from A–D; a search icon is a separate rule.',5:'Preserve semantic color; standardize touch size and a non-color selected cue.',6:'Keep explicit panel-grid roles; select a common tile geometry where the job matches.',7:'Keep purposeful person/place/topic cues, but give repeated navigation jobs consistent spacing and touch targets.',8:'Keep native-select behavior and grid behavior; standardize minimum hit area before decorative details.',9:'Preserve tab/switch/slider semantics rather than replacing them with ordinary buttons.',10:'Increase small expand/inspect hit areas while keeping the visual hierarchy.',11:'Give reset/secondary actions less emphasis than final Apply/Show results actions.',12:'Fix phone hit areas before choosing circle versus rounded-square decoration.',13:'Keep title and multiline roles distinct while aligning common borders/focus cues.',14:'Keep centered and bottom-sheet layouts when useful; align close targets and spacing within each.',15:'Mix preferred shells and preferred internals with explicit usage rules.',16:'Use a clear shared keyboard cue, including wrapper focus where needed.'}
lines=['**TL;DR:** The comparison boards are ready. They bring together the independently discovered controls, cards and panels—not just your examples—so you can choose useful elements from either generation. Keep one, several or all styles per group and say where each should be used. No choices are assumed and no app files changed.','',f'**[Open the complete comparison worksheet](comparison-boards.html)** — 16 groups, {len(x["families"])} source-component families and {len(x["boards"])} image sheets. Each group includes an expandable gallery of every captured appearance, its location, dimensions, colors, selectors and source lines. Families are not a claim that every family has a unique visual skin.','', '**How to answer:** `D4 keep A,C; A for search boxes, C’s magnifier on all searches. D2 keep B,I for direct passages and C,F,H for citations.` Letter IDs belong to their group. You may select individual appearances in the HTML gallery if you want a particular theme/state example, rather than the whole family. Nothing in the worksheet changes the app. Download selections before closing it, or reply in chat.','', '**Benefits and tradeoffs:** One style within a matching job is easiest to recognize but may remove useful page cues. Several styles with clear usage rules preserve useful differences but need maintenance. Keeping every current style changes no controls, but leaves the documented usability issues. All these style choices are reversible; a 44px touch-target/focus pass can be chosen independently. Any app-wide P2 redesign remains outside this review.','', '**Scope:** The original control matrix covers dark/light and desktop/phone at 100% text. New rich-object captures retain your 115% setting and are labeled separately. Source-only, account-only, native-only and unforced-error states are identified in [coverage-gaps.md](coverage-gaps.md); they are not passed off as live screenshots.','']
for g,fs in groups.items():
 lines+=['### D'+str(g)+' — '+T[g],'',intent[g],'']
 for b in x['boards']:
  if b['group']==g:lines.append(f'[Comparison sheet {b["part"]}: {", ".join(b["options"])}]({b["image"]})')
